  "origin": "original",
  "configuration": "June1942 Soryu: narrow cruiser-derived hull, starboard island forward of amidships, two downturned starboard funnels, three elevators, six twin127mm positions and fourteen twin25mm positions. No radar.",
  "accuracy": "Independently authored detailed exterior reconstruction for the June1942 demonstration. Major class configuration is source-backed. Hull body sections, small station offsets, doors, rails and plating are inferred original artwork. Not a recovered shipyard model and not a claim that every small AA fitting or paint patch is exact. One stored GLB supplies every view; no interior is modeled.",
  "geometrySource": "New class-specific full exterior and station ledger. No campaign carrier mesh or previous vertex buffer is reused.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "US Naval Technical Mission to Japan, A-11, January1946, TableI printed p8",
      "url": "https://www.fischer-tropsch.org/primary_documents/gvt_reports/USNAVY/USNTMJ%20Reports/USNTMJ-200A-0560-0608%20Report%20A-11.pdf",
      "license": "Factual reference only; original mesh and surface detail. Source illustration not redistributed or traced.",
      "usedFor": "Soryu/Hiryu dimensions, differing flight-deck width and three elevators. Read with NHHC archival photographs; draught and body sections are separately stated estimates."
    },
    {
      "title": "NHHC archival Soryu photograph NH73061 / USAF ID4845",
      "url": "https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/OnlineLibrary/photos/sh-fornv/japan/japsh-s/soryu.htm",
      "license": "Factual reference only; original mesh and surface detail. Source illustration not redistributed or traced.",
      "usedFor": "Inspected archival photograph NH73061 / USAF ID4845: island side/longitudinal station, flight-deck overhang, hangar massing and funnel arrangement. Midway photographs corroborate the overall fit; fine fittings are inferred."
    }
  ],
